# Three players: "as though they didn't have hexproof" is about the creatures, so it is not only Bot1's spells that may target
# Bot2's hexproof Sylvan Caryatid while Bot1's Nowhere to Run is out. On turn three, with no Nowhere to Run yet, Bot3's
# Lightning Bolt is refused at the Caryatid (the control). On turn four Bot1 casts Nowhere to Run (its trigger takes Bot3's
# Ornithopter); then Bot2's Bolt is refused at Bot1's own hexproof Caryatid (Bot1 controls it, so it is not one of the creatures
# Bot1's opponents control) and Bot3's Bolt is aimed at Bot2's Caryatid and kills it.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Sylvan Caryatid
Swamp
Nowhere to Run
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Sylvan Caryatid
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x12

[Bot3 Deck]
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Mountain x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sylvan Caryatid.Cast
[T3 Bot3.Main1]
Bot3.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot3.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
! Bot3.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
[T4 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Nowhere to Run.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter)
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot3.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot3.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid)
Bot3.Pass
[T4 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Sylvan Caryatid
Bot3.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield.Sylvan Caryatid.Damage = 0
